{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic","id":1171553,"title":"Can an Awakening be predicted with magic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-29T09:50:45-08:00","id":1171553,"title":"Can an Awakening be predicted with magic?","content":"What the title said. Is it possible with any combination of Arcana, Attainments or other supernatural abilities? If not, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T09:57:17-08:00","id":1171555,"title":"","content":"Short answer yes, but not with a 100% accuracy rating because the future is mutable.<br /> <br /> It\u2019d only take Time, Divination if you\u2019re just asking, Prophecy if you\u2019re trying to engineer it. Fate would also work for the latter method. Probably still tends to turn out Banishers more often than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 12-29-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T10:48:38-08:00","id":1171566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1171555#post1171555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer yes, but not with a 100% accuracy rating because the future is mutable.<br /> <br /> It\u2019d only take Time, Divination if you\u2019re just asking, Prophecy if you\u2019re trying to engineer it. Fate would also work for the latter method. Probably still tends to turn out Banishers more often than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks a lot!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T11:07:21-08:00","id":1171570,"title":"","content":"The Gaurdians specialize in using their Labyrinth to find people who might Awaken by the way, they probably use magic, but they seem to be just as good at mundanely noticing the patterns that people who are likely to Awaken soon end up following. <br /> <br /> SOS is also supposed to have a section dealing with Mages who go out of their way to interfere with Awakenings which implies they\u2019re possible to detect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T14:29:25-08:00","id":1171627,"title":"","content":"They're possible to detect when in progress, but not predict - Time magic to look into someone's future shows them as a Sleeper or Sleepwalker until they Awaken, at which point their future changes to be a mage. The reasons are metaphysical and imply something about what an Awakening <i>is</i> that the Orders chew over.<br /> <br /> You can look for the sort of people who might Awaken, though, and that's where the Awakening-spotters in the Orders operate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T15:16:03-08:00","id":1171640,"title":"","content":"I stand corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T16:08:05-08:00","id":1171657,"title":"","content":"In my campaign, I wrote in a Guardian who specialized in finding those who have already Awakened, but instead of being a candidate, or in a Labyrinth/Cryptopolis/what-have-you, they were completely alone. She would use a combination of Fate and Prime to find them; Prime to discern, amd Fate to reach them just in time to introduce them to the Pentacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:35:21-08:00","id":1171859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1171627#post1171627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're possible to detect when in progress, but not predict - Time magic to look into someone's future shows them as a Sleeper or Sleepwalker until they Awaken, at which point their future changes to be a mage. The reasons are metaphysical and imply something about what an Awakening <i>is</i> that the Orders chew over.<br /> <br /> You can look for the sort of people who might Awaken, though, and that's where the Awakening-spotters in the Orders operate.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo can Fate be used to arrange to be present during the Awakening of a random stranger?<br /> \u200bThis quote makes it sound like Awakenings are enough of a break off from Fallen World reality that they are hidden from Fate and Time until after they branch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T13:20:49-08:00","id":1171873,"title":"","content":"No, because they're enough of a break from Fallen reality that they're hidden from... What you just said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T13:46:40-08:00","id":1171879,"title":"","content":"It makes me wonder, is it possible to predict with Time or Fate (or other Arcana) on archmastery levels?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T04:06:44-08:00","id":1171987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1171879#post1171879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes me wonder, is it possible to predict with Time or Fate (or other Arcana) on archmastery levels?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Prime 7 (Practice of Entities) can Awaken someone, although it draws the attention of the Exarchs and usually creates a Banisher.<br /> <br /> I suppose a similar argument could be made for at least Fate. Engineer events that cause the person to Awaken (or at least start the process). Most of what archmages can do is up to the Storyteller anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:08:10-08:00","id":1172785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1171627#post1171627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're possible to detect when in progress, but not predict - Time magic to look into someone's future shows them as a Sleeper or Sleepwalker until they Awaken, at which point their future changes to be a mage. The reasons are metaphysical and imply something about what an Awakening <i>is</i> that the Orders chew over.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good Obsession for a Time mage would be closely reading the future to see which mundane Sleepers keep inexplicably showing up at future magical events. I'm picturing an NPC who's exhaustively charted the life and works of an anonymous person who hasn't yet Awakened, but is inferred to exist from future historical context.<br /> <br /> e: a happy accident here is that Awakened history becomes harder to reliably predict because divination can't account for everyone who will be involved. Imagine a Seer steepling his fingers and warning her underlings that &quot;things are not proceeding as i have foreseen&quot; because your newly-Awakened PCs are throwing wrenches into prophecies years in the making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 01-02-2018, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T00:03:40-08:00","id":1174480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1171627#post1171627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're possible to detect when in progress, but not predict - Time magic to look into someone's future shows them as a Sleeper or Sleepwalker until they Awaken, at which point their future changes to be a mage. The reasons are metaphysical and imply something about what an Awakening <i>is</i> that the Orders chew over.<br /> <br /> You can look for the sort of people who might Awaken, though, and that's where the Awakening-spotters in the Orders operate.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you would actually work to map out the future of a sleeper who will eventually awaken, you would see them leading a normal sleeper life, and then when they awaken that future you saw is suddenly obsolete and replaced with their new future as an Awakened?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T02:57:29-08:00","id":1174506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aristarkos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1174480#post1174480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you would actually work to map out the future of a sleeper who will eventually awaken, you would see them leading a normal sleeper life, and then when they awaken that future you saw is suddenly obsolete and replaced with their new future as an Awakened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T14:07:55-08:00","id":1174645,"title":"","content":"So is almost as if (or just is) that awakenings also cause Aponeia, as happens with archmasters though to a much lesser degree since it seems it only affects your potential future not your past retroactively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-09-2018, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T14:55:06-08:00","id":1174665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1174645#post1174645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is almost as if (or just is) that awakenings also cause Aponeia, as happens with archmasters though to a much lesser degree since it seems it only affects your potential future not your past retroactively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense if you think about it. Archmasters have to impose a filter bubble on the Supernal to keep themselves from being obliterated by it when doing a Supernal working, and the Watchtowers are basically just a bigger version of that which can be accessed by soon-to-be former Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T12:49:52-08:00","id":1174955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1174645#post1174645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is almost as if (or just is) that awakenings also cause Aponeia, as happens with archmasters though to a much lesser degree since it seems it only affects your potential future not your past retroactively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this is what metamorphic Awakenings are all about?<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"> Signs of Sorcery [Mage: The Awakening] [Open Development] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T04:41:03-08:00","id":1176487,"title":"","content":"In my headcanon, Awakenings are acts of Imperium by the Rank 10 entity known as The Watchtowers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T04:51:59-08:00","id":1176489,"title":"","content":"Isn't it semi-vaguely-sorta-canonical that the Watchtowers are the Cintamanis of the Oracles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T06:00:55-08:00","id":1176498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1176489#post1176489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it semi-vaguely-sorta-canonical that the Watchtowers are the Cintamanis of the Oracles?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might be, if the Oracles are real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T10:01:06-08:00","id":1176537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1176487#post1176487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my headcanon, Awakenings are acts of Imperium by the Rank 10 entity known as The Watchtowers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not headcanon. They are.<br /> <br /> (The Watchtowers are Talismans - extrusions of some other higher power that manifest in the Supernal and form the Lustrums around Awakenings-in-progress so new mages don't get obliterated by being in the Supernal. Which raises the question - extrusions of <i>what</i>? Even if nothing else about them is real, many archmasters regard &quot;Oracle&quot; as meaning &quot;whoever it was that created the Paths&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T11:14:54-08:00","id":1176555,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;extrusions FROM what&quot; is more intriguing to me than &quot;extrusions OF what&quot;. Are Talismans produced by other Supernal entities? Or do they come from outside, like an Archmaster's Lustrum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T11:18:30-08:00","id":1176556,"title":"","content":"A Talisman is like an Ochemata, but also like an Artifact - it's a magic item that is also a subsoul of whoever made it.<br /> <br /> Or kinda like the One Ring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T12:21:01-08:00","id":1176566,"title":"","content":"One Tower to rule them all, One Tower to find them; One Tower to Awaken them all<br /> and to the Supernal bind them.*<br /> <br /> * Translated from High Speech inscribed on a small toroidal formation of unknown material in lines of temperature approximately measured at 10^29 Kelvin. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T13:14:21-08:00","id":1176583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1176537#post1176537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not headcanon. They are.<br /> <br /> (The Watchtowers are Talismans - extrusions of some other higher power that manifest in the Supernal and form the Lustrums around Awakenings-in-progress so new mages don't get obliterated by being in the Supernal. Which raises the question - extrusions of <i>what</i>? )</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, of the Principle, of course! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3709-doktorniemand","name":"DoktorNiemand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T13:35:32-08:00","id":1176587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1176566#post1176566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Tower to rule them all, One Tower to find them; One Tower to Awaken them all and to the Supernal bind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This message has been approved by the Tremere council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T15:05:08-08:00","id":1176613,"title":"","content":"Maybe extrusions of Annunaki, after all Mages can't create paradox if they get destroyed during awakenings. <br /> <br /> I think it'd be a great twist, the Oracles are Annunaki and the Watch Towers are effectly the Supernal reflection of the Ziggurats, not the other way around. <br /> <br /> It means if discovered that all Mages are Scelusi, without realizing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T00:35:39-08:00","id":1176714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1176613#post1176613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe extrusions of Annunaki, after all Mages can't create paradox if they get destroyed during awakenings.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be a great twist, the Oracles are Annunaki and the Watch Towers are effectly the Supernal reflection of the Ziggurats, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> It means if discovered that all Mages are Scelusi, without realizing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, the Greek Mythos in To The Strongest suggests that to awaken a mage has to gain assistance from the 'Titans', beings that live in the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T00:46:31-08:00","id":1176716,"title":"","content":"Even if you can't predict Awakenings, you can still time travel into the past knowing who will awaken the next day, week, year, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T05:01:28-08:00","id":1176924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1176537#post1176537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The Watchtowers are Talismans - extrusions of some other higher power that manifest in the Supernal and form the Lustrums around Awakenings-in-progress so new mages don't get obliterated by being in the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it sounds like Watchtowers are an external force (which we knew, I suppose) that interfere with Awakenings to make them safer for the person Awakening, which leads me to wonder, &quot;What happens to an 'unprotected' Awakening?&quot;<br /> <br /> Is the 'default' state of Awakening without Watchtower interference just that everyone is a Pathless Banisher? I mean, I'm sure the answer would be more complicated than that anyway, if it were the case. Or just maybe Awakenings wouldn't happen without the Watchtowers anyway. It does give me an image of Mages in the Sundered World Era where there's some turning point of Mages gaining a Path and the Wisdom trait, although I don't know when it would happen since time is kinda still rebuilding itself in that Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T05:17:24-08:00","id":1176928,"title":"","content":"It seems like the unprotected awakening thing would be a lot like becoming an archmage. Though since your physical body wouldn't be entering the supernal it would probably be just your mind being unmade on failure, leaving your body completely empty. Also I guess they'd have to build a lustrum for just their mind? Probably wouldn't be able to do it. <br /> <br /> Most likely it isn't something that normally happens though, even relative to awakening itself. <br /> <br /> Question related to the OP: Can it be predicted if and when a sleeper will become a sleepwalker? Or some other supernatural template?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T02:31:48-08:00","id":1178014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1171553-can-an-awakening-be-predicted-with-magic?p=1176928#post1176928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like the unprotected awakening thing would be a lot like becoming an archmage. Though since your physical body wouldn't be entering the supernal it would probably be just your mind being unmade on failure, leaving your body completely empty. Also I guess they'd have to build a lustrum for just their mind? Probably wouldn't be able to do it.<br /> <br /> Most likely it isn't something that normally happens though, even relative to awakening itself.<br /> <br /> Question related to the OP: Can it be predicted if and when a sleeper will become a sleepwalker? Or some other supernatural template?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the way that other templates are treated in relation to Time magic, I would say you could easily predict supernatural transformations that are not inherent to the character. Reading the future might say on this day, person X will be walking in an alley and Embraced by a vampire. Same for changelings. For transformations that are inherent to the character, it might be a bit more dicey and depend on the template itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}